       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled daily dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for IR)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided into doses\n\nIf the 1,700 mg three times daily dose is intentional, tell me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy first. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
